---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="About Zeynep — The Local Stop" bodyClass="trip">
  <div class="wrap">
    <a class="back" href="/">← back to the map</a>
  </div>

  <header class="wrap">
    <span class="when">Meet the person behind this site</span>
    <h1>About Zeynep</h1>
    <div class="washi"></div>
  </header>

  <div class="wrap about-page">
    <div class="polaroid">
      <div class="tape"></div>
      <div class="photo">
        <img src="/Assets/Zeynep.jpg" alt="Zeynep" loading="lazy">
      </div>
    </div>

    <div class="about-page__text">
      <p>
        <em>[Placeholder — this whole page is yours to rewrite. A few prompts to get you started below; delete whatever you don't use.]</em>
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>How it started:</b> [when did you catch the travel bug — a first solo trip, a move abroad, something else?]
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>What "like a local" means to me:</b> [why non-touristy spots, what you're allergic to in typical travel guides, what you actually look for in a place.]
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>Where I am now:</b> [home base, how many countries/continents so far if you want to lead with a number, what's next on the list.]
      </p>
      <p>
        <b>Why this site exists:</b> a running notebook of the streets, the small rituals, and the things I'd tell a friend before they landed — from every trip I take.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>

  <footer class="wrap">
    <span class="hand">à bientôt, quelque part ✧</span>
    <p style="margin-top:8px;font-size:.85rem"><a href="/" style="color:var(--terra)">← back to the map</a></p>
  </footer>
</BaseLayout>
